		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499678329028-101435549a4e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1449824913935-59a10b8d2000?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515542622106-78bda8ba0e5b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526170375885-4d8ecf77b99f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1455390582262-044cdead277a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516035069371-29a1b244cc32?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531297484001-80022131f5a1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
		<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=60" alt="">
	</div>
	<span class="im-poster-shade im-poster-shade-full"></span>
	<strong class="im-poster-word im-poster-word-lg im-poster-on-media">october<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
	<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-paper">12 cities · 31 days</span>
	<span class="im-poster-time">32:17</span>
</figure>
{{/example}}
<p><b>Use when</b> the video gathers many moments. <b>Why it works</b>: twelve tiles read as "a lot happened" without anyone needing to see any one of them, so the tint can be heavy and the word can be the biggest on any type. <b>Avoid</b> fewer than eight tiles — then each one is looked at, and none is big enough to be seen.</p>

<h2 id="type">Type only</h2>
{{#example}}
<figure class="im-poster im-poster-type">
	<strong class="im-poster-word">I stopped<br>posting daily<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
	<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-ink">an essay</span>
	<span class="im-poster-time">12:44</span>
</figure>
{{/example}}
<p><b>Use when</b> the idea is the subject and any picture would be a stock photo. <b>Why it works</b>: in a feed of faces and colour, a white tile with two black lines is the quietest thing on the screen, and quiet stands out. It is the one type where the word may run to five words, because there is nothing else to read. <b>Avoid</b> using it twice in a row; its power is being the exception.</p>

<h2 id="product">Product</h2>
{{#example}}
<figure class="im-poster im-poster-product">
	<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-round" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526170375885-4d8ecf77b99f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=700&q=75" alt="">
	<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-ink">₹9,999 · worth it?</span>
	<span class="im-poster-disc">{{icon "arrow-right"}}</span>
	<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-arch" src="/assets/brand/portrait.jpg" alt="">
	<span class="im-poster-time">15:29</span>
</figure>
{{/example}}
<p><b>Use when</b> the video judges one thing. <b>Why it works</b>: the circle isolates the product the way a studio shot would, the arrow points from the thing to the person, and the price-and-question chip is the whole promise — so this type has no word at all. <b>Avoid</b> brand logos in the frame bigger than the product; a thumbnail is not an advert for somebody else.</p>
